lb-9lnz.description:
Add optional TuiSender field to Logger and new methods:

  pub struct Logger {
      writer: SharedWriter,
      tui: Option<TuiSender>,  // new
  }

  impl Logger {
      // existing new() unchanged (tui: None)
      pub fn with_tui(path: &Path, tui: TuiSender) -> io::Result<Self>
      pub fn with_label(&self, label: &str) -> Self  // clone with different pane label, shared file writer

      // Modified:
      pub fn log(&self, msg: &str)  // → TUI if present, else eprintln!; always writes to file
      pub fn display(&self, msg: &str)  // → TUI if present, else println!; does NOT write to file
      pub fn tee_stderr(&self, ...)  // drain to TUI if present, else eprintln!; always writes to file
      pub fn tee_stdout(&self, ...)  // same pattern
  }

  impl TuiSender {
      pub fn with_label(&self, label: &str) -> Self  // clone with new pane label, same tx
  }

The with_label() method on Logger creates a clone that shares the same file writer (Arc<Mutex<...>>) but routes to a different TUI pane. Used for concurrent summary/decider stages.
